    "testedMachine": "Two directly connected DGX Spark systems (--sparks 2) or four cabled as a daisy chain (--sparks 4)",
    "notes": [
      "Candidate: SparkGLM 0.3.4. At TP-2 with dflash2 it qualified on 2026-11-14 against 0.3.3 on the same pair: identical greedy output and prompt logprobs, 109/109 live checks, and one RigMark round level with 0.3.3 (prose 38.8 against 38.1 tok/s, cold 16K prefill 2,849 against 2,865); a thinking-off JSON-schema call went from 19-27 s to about 3 s. Strict mode, vision and TP-4 were not run.",
      "With --sparks 2 the pair uses tensor and expert parallelism 2 across the private ConnectX RoCE fabric; each node needs cluster.nodes[ID].fabricHca and fabricInterface. With --sparks 4 the ranks follow cluster.nodes[ID].fabricChain on a switchless chain, rank 0 leads, and the workers start from the far end.",
      "Every Spark reserves 114 GiB with a 4096 MiB OOM guard. TP-2 raises GPU memory utilization to 0.91 with the display carveout and shards KV across the pair; TP-4 uses the profile's 0.88 with neither, and leaves no room for sidecars.",
      "The disk prefix cache is 48 GB at TP-2 and off at TP-4, where it is not qualified.",
      "Licenses: the Atlas engine in the image is AGPL-3.0-only (not included in LLooM). The v81 and v80 drafters are Enntity's, from a private repository; incoai/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2 is Apache-2.0 from the pinned revision 6cc6c481; nvidia/GLM-5.3-Flash-FP4-Local is under the NVIDIA Open Model Agreement (base model MIT).",
      "All Sparks must carry the same pins, the same backend directory, the same checkpoint and drafter, and LLooM configs that name the same cluster leader."
    ]
  },
